- Benefit sustained in long-term follow-up beyond 12 months (test for heterogeneity p=0.60)

**Key Clinical Findings Summary:**
1. Cotrimoxazole prophylaxis significantly reduces mortality in HIV-infected children (43% relative risk reduction)
2. The mortality benefit is sustained over time and consistent across all ages and immune status levels
3. Safety profile is comparable between treatment and placebo arms
4. Very rare detection of Pneumocystis pneumonia in treated patients
5. Strong recommendation for use in resource-poor settings regardless of local resistance patterns

